rwtest 1
test "Withered soul hurts" project=Bernael group=Genes created=2026-09-19T00:00:00

requires dlc=Biotech
spawn Pawn:Colonist at 0,0 name="Bernael" xenotype=BX_Bernael
assert pawn "Bernael" hediff=BX_WitheredSoulHediff expect=present

# "hediff=" answers whether the hediff is on the pawn, "visible" how it is
# shown - two different questions. Every stage of this def used to carry
# becomeVisible false, so up to 35% pain came out of a line that stood nowhere.
# The three stages with a painOffset show themselves now. The fourth carries
# becomeVisible false and hides it all the same - why, stands below, at the line
# that checks it.
#
# This used to need select + tab "Health" + assert text on the label. That hangs
# on the label instead of on the def and checks whether the tab is open along
# the way; "visible" names the def and puts the stage in the report as well.
give "Bernael" need=Mood value=0.1
tick 480 reason="Hediff_SeverityBasedOnNeed reads the need every 420 ticks"
assert pawn "Bernael" pain min=0.32 max=0.42
# Visible while it hurts - and this line stands before the negation further
# down on purpose: both directions in the same file.
assert pawn "Bernael" hediff=BX_WitheredSoulHediff visible expect=present
give "Bernael" need=Mood value=0.7
tick 480 reason="same interval, one stage up"
assert pawn "Bernael" pain min=0.12 max=0.22
give "Bernael" need=Mood value=0.95
tick 480 reason="same interval, into the stage that carries no offset"
assert pawn "Bernael" pain max=0.08
# No pain - and still visible, although this stage is the only one carrying
# becomeVisible false. That is not a bug in the mod, it is
# Verse.Hediff.Visible:
#
#     if (!visible && CurStage != null) return CurStage.becomeVisible;
#     return true;
#
# "visible" is a field there, not an expression. Hediff.Tick sets it to true
# once, as soon as the hediff has been visible, and scribes it into the save.
# The def starts at initialSeverity 1 in exactly this stage and is hidden there;
# the "give need=Mood value=0.1" line at the top sends it past stage 0, and from
# then on the one-way street has been driven. becomeVisible false means "does
# not become visible for the first time here", not "is hidden again".
#
# This line stood as expect=absent until 2026-09-20 and was red, because it
# asked the engine for something the engine cannot do. If the hediff really is
# meant to disappear again, that is a change to the mod and not a fix: override
# Visible in Hediff_SeverityBasedOnNeed and return CurStage.becomeVisible
# directly. Until then <becomeVisible>false</becomeVisible> in the def's last
# stage is dead weight, and this line says what actually happens.
assert pawn "Bernael" hediff=BX_WitheredSoulHediff visible expect=present
assert log clean
